{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Every programmer makes these mistakes. The difference between a beginner and an experienced engineer is mostly that the experienced one **expects** them, and checks for them before they cause trouble. Here are the ones that bite most often with arrays."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Off-by-one: stepping past the end"
